n Predictions","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/us-presidential-election-predictions/270025","site":"T Nation · 3253 posts · 2020"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Tie clip — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tie_clip"},{"title":"Tie clip / tie bar — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Tie_clip"},{"title":"Tie clip - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tie_clip"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Grooming","chain":["Clip holds tie flat against shirt","Tie stays straight in motion","Outfit looks neater and more finished"],"effect":"direct","text":"The clip keeps the tie in place so the outfit stays tidy through the day and adds a small metal accent."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Tie clip","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tie_clip"},"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Tie_clip","lead":["A tie clip, tie bar or tie clasp is a small, usually metal accessory that fastens a necktie to the shirt front.[1][2] It stops the tie from swinging or dangling and adds a decorative accent.[2]","It became popular in the 1920s with thin silk ties and largely replaced the older tie pin.[1] In the United States a tie clip is one of the few pieces of jewellery service members may wear.[1]","No clinical or scientific studies have examined tie clips as an appearance aid."],"infobox":[["Type","Menswear accessory"],["Popularised","1920s"],["Materials","Sterling silver, gold, brass, steel"],["Related","Tie pin, tie tack"],["Typical placement","A few inches below the knot, per Grokipedia"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["The modern clip has a spring-loaded jaw that grips tie and shirt without piercing, unlike tie tacks or pins that go through the fabric.[2] Many carry engraving, monograms or club badges.[1][2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Tie pins and stick pins preceded the clip in the nineteenth century.[2] Straight silk ties became fashionable in the 1920s and made non-piercing clips preferable, according to Grokipedia, which is AI-generated; it adds that the style surged after the Second World War and faded with casual dress in the 1960s and 70s.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1920s","event":"Tie clips become popular with thin silk ties.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Tie clip","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tie_clip","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Tie clip (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Tie_clip","source":"Grokipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"MarkKO's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/markkos-training-log/208986","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/264067","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 2)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-2/273731","site":"T Nation · 8490 posts · 2021"},{"title":"10 Miles Back Again","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/10-miles-back-again/249635","site":"T Nation · 7474 posts · 2018"},{"title":"Things That Piss You Off","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-piss-you-off/163775","site":"T Nation · 7426 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Becoming Canis dirus - SvenG's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/becoming-canis-dirus-svengs-training-log/273583","site":"T Nation · 6787 posts · 2021"}]}